WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:06.100
Arriving just weeks before Avengers: Endgame
hits the big screen, Captain Marvel's origin

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:10.500
story is crucial to understanding how the
surviving Avengers will regroup and take down

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:12.150
the Mad Titan Thanos.

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:16.020
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and now
that Captain Marvel's movie is out, we've

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:19.570
got some juicy details on her powers and where
they come from.

00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:23.230
And when you dig deeper, there's some very
compelling evidence hidden in the Marvel canon

00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:28.660
about how Carol Danvers' very particular power
set will be key to defeating Thanos in Avengers:

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:29.660
Endgame.

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:32.711
Obviously there's spoilers ahead for Captain
Marvel, so take care if you haven't seen it

00:00:32.711 --> 00:00:33.711
yet.

00:00:33.711 --> 00:00:38.000
The big reveal in Captain Marvel is that Carol
Danvers acquires her extraordinary powers

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:42.220
when she blows up an engine that was created
using power from the Tesseract.

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:46.290
Carol destroys the experimental light speed
engine to prevent the technology falling into

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:50.890
the hands of the Kree, but when the device
explodes, Carol's body absorbs the energy

00:00:50.890 --> 00:00:53.489
which imbues her with superhuman powers.

00:00:53.489 --> 00:00:58.100
After Carol gets knocked out from the blast,
she's abducted by the Kree and taken to Hala

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:02.579
as Yon-Rogg sees her powers as a means of
accessing the power of the Tesseract.

00:01:02.579 --> 00:01:06.520
Carol gets an infusion of Kree blood which
crucially gives her additional powers that

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:10.330
the Kree enjoy such as super-strength, durability
and stamina.

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:15.080
Remember, for example, in Guardians of the
Galaxy, the Kree Ronan was able to hold one

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:18.710
of the Infinity Stones directly in his own
hands without any injury.

00:01:18.710 --> 00:01:23.370
So, Carol Danvers not only has a glowing Iron
Fist that can emit photon blasts, but she

00:01:23.370 --> 00:01:28.420
also has a hidden power set that remains locked
away until the end of the movie.

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:32.170
When she realises that the Kree have been
deliberately holding her back and dampening

00:01:32.170 --> 00:01:37.340
her powers via the chip in her neck, she pulls
it out unleashing her full powers.

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:41.710
In the final showdown between Carol and Ronan,
we see the full power set she absorbed from

00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:43.520
the Tesseract on display.

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:48.000
She can smash through a series of ballistic
warheads Superman-style as well as completely

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:52.800
take out an enormous Kree battleship with
ease, plus she can now fly though space and

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:55.890
survive without the need of protection from
a spaceship.

00:01:55.890 --> 00:01:59.970
In the comics, these abilities are referred
to as Binary powers which give her access

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:06.080
to the energies of a white hole and therefore
the ability to control heat, gravity and electromagnetism.

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:11.279
So, how will Carol Danvers' Tesseract powers
help her and the Avengers defeat Thanos?

00:02:11.279 --> 00:02:15.540
Well, for the answer to that, we need to think
back to another Marvel character who also

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:18.090
derives her powers from an Infinity Stone.

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:22.219
In the post-credits scene of Captain America:
The Winter Soldier, we got our first introduction

00:02:22.219 --> 00:02:24.200
to Scarlet Witch and Quicksilver.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:28.249
HYDRA were using the power of the Mind Stone,
which was contained in Loki's Sceptre, to

00:02:28.249 --> 00:02:31.659
experiment on the twins giving them superhuman
abilities.

00:02:31.659 --> 00:02:35.959
Scarlet Witch showed off some of these powers
in some truly badass moments during Infinity

00:02:35.959 --> 00:02:36.959
War.

00:02:36.959 --> 00:02:41.049
But more crucially she also used her powers
in a last-ditch attempt to stop Thanos from

00:02:41.049 --> 00:02:45.760
collecting all six Infinity Stones when she
destroyed the Mind Stone lodged in Vision's

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:48.370
forehead, at least temporarily.

00:02:48.370 --> 00:02:52.239
Because Wanda's powers originate in the Mind
Stone she was the only one in the Avengers

00:02:52.239 --> 00:02:53.800
team who could perform this task.

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:56.859
"I've been giving a good deal of thought to
this entity in my head."

00:02:56.859 --> 00:02:57.920
"About its nature.

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:00.809
But also its composition."

00:03:00.809 --> 00:03:06.730
"I think if it were exposed to a sufficiently
powerful energy source... something very similar

00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:12.340
to its own signature, perhaps... its molecular
integrity could fail."

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:16.779
And that's exactly why it's so important that
Carol Danvers received her powers from the

00:03:16.779 --> 00:03:18.659
Tesseract, aka the Space Stone.

00:03:18.659 --> 00:03:23.469
If we look at what Scarlet Witch was able
to do to the Mind Stone in Infinity War, we

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:27.439
can assume that Captain Marvel could do something
similar to the Space Stone in Endgame.

00:03:27.439 --> 00:03:32.579
For example, Carol's photon blasts likely
have an energy signature similar or identical

00:03:32.579 --> 00:03:37.329
to the Space Stone which currently sits in
Thanos's Infinity Gauntlet, so she could therefore

00:03:37.329 --> 00:03:41.170
destroy the Space Stone when she goes up against
Thanos in Endgame.

00:03:41.170 --> 00:03:45.299
Wrecking the Space Stone could severely hinder
Thanos, for starters by preventing him from

00:03:45.299 --> 00:03:47.839
teleporting between locations.

00:03:47.839 --> 00:03:52.069
On top of that, in Infinity War, we witnessed
how the Mad Titan used the Space Stone in

00:03:52.069 --> 00:03:55.659
combination with other Infinity Stones to
particularly lethal effect.

00:03:55.659 --> 00:04:00.969
For example, he used it with the Power Stone
to tear apart Titan's moon and rain down meteors

00:04:00.969 --> 00:04:02.590
onto the heroes.

00:04:02.590 --> 00:04:06.659
In Wakanda, Thanos employed the Space Stone
to make Banner's Hulkbuster phase through

00:04:06.659 --> 00:04:09.189
him and then encased him in rock.

00:04:09.189 --> 00:04:14.040
Thanos also used it as a defence against ammo
from War Machine as well as Scarlet Witch's

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:15.249
energy blasts.

00:04:15.249 --> 00:04:19.790
And he also used it early in the film to freeze
Loki's arm and dagger when the God of Mischief

00:04:19.790 --> 00:04:23.060
tried to double-cross the Mad Titan and kill
him.

00:04:23.060 --> 00:04:26.820
Which means the loss of this particular stone
would leave Thanos vulnerable against some

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:29.060
attacks he'd previously been able to withstand.

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:34.600
And, if this time, Thor or someone else landed
a potentially deadly blow on the Mad Titan,

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:38.720
he wouldn't be able to portal himself away
like he did in Infinity War.

00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:43.030
What's especially interesting also is that,
in the comics, a former Captain Marvel once

00:04:43.030 --> 00:04:47.250
destroyed the comic book equivalent of the
Tesseract when it was in the hands of Thanos.

00:04:47.250 --> 00:04:51.670
In the comics, Captain Marvel's a superhero
moniker that's been taken up by many individuals

00:04:51.670 --> 00:04:57.170
before Carol Danvers, and the very first Captain
Marvel was the alien Kree warrior Mar-Vell.

00:04:57.170 --> 00:05:02.880
In Captain Marvel #33, after acquiring the
Cosmic Cube, Thanos gained dominion and control

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:03.880
over the universe.

00:05:03.880 --> 00:05:08.790
However, Mar-Vell, aka Captain Marvel, was
able to destroy the Cosmic Cube, removing

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:12.460
the power that Thanos had acquired and restoring
the universe.

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:16.590
Connecting these clues, I can see it's likely
we'll see Captain Marvel destroy or disable

00:05:16.590 --> 00:05:18.110
the Space Stone in Endgame.

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:22.820
And it could well be that this is the moment
when the Avengers get the upper hand on Thanos

00:05:22.820 --> 00:05:25.420
and defeat him once and for all.

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:29.580
Destroying the Space Stone would hold some
special resonance in the MCU as the Tesseract

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:33.590
was our first introduction to the power of
the Infinity Stones and has played a major

00:05:33.590 --> 00:05:35.410
role throughout the franchise.

00:05:35.410 --> 00:05:39.970
In Captain America: The First Avenger, when
Red Skull tried to handle the Tesseract directly,

00:05:39.970 --> 00:05:44.350
the artefact opened up a portal and banished
the villain to Vormir where he was cursed

00:05:44.350 --> 00:05:46.330
to watch over the Soul Stone.

00:05:46.330 --> 00:05:50.830
The Tesseract was also a major part of the
first Avengers movie and, of course, it made

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:55.190
an important reappearance when Loki stole
it again in Thor: Ragnarok and then had to

00:05:55.190 --> 00:05:57.350
hand it over to Thanos in Infinity War.

00:05:57.350 --> 00:06:02.230
So, it would be especially fitting if Marvel
ended this phase of its cinematic universe

00:06:02.230 --> 00:06:07.060
by destroying the very first macguffin that
has taken the fans on this epic journey.

00:06:07.060 --> 00:06:11.240
The one problem with this is that if Captain
Marvel does destroy the Space Stone, then

00:06:11.240 --> 00:06:15.111
Thanos could simply wind the clock back with
the Time Stone like he did with Scarlet Witch

00:06:15.111 --> 00:06:17.040
to restore the Mind Stone.

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:18.040
But...

00:06:18.040 --> 00:06:21.500
Thanos may not be able to repeat that trick
in Endgame.

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:25.580
After all, the Infinity Gauntlet was damaged
during the snap and the Time Stone may well

00:06:25.580 --> 00:06:26.580
have been affected.

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:30.940
Plus, we don't know what the consequences
might be for Thanos having meddled with time

00:06:30.940 --> 00:06:34.730
in Infinity War, and there could be something
that will stop him doing that again.

00:06:34.730 --> 00:06:38.970
Remember, after all, that Doctor Strange was
told in his movie that there are consequences

00:06:38.970 --> 00:06:43.150
for messing around with time:
"You still think there will be no consequences,

00:06:43.150 --> 00:06:44.300
Strange?"

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:46.440
"No price to pay?"

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:49.220
"We broke our rules, just like her."

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:51.630
"The bill comes due.

00:06:51.630 --> 00:06:52.630
Always!

00:06:52.630 --> 00:06:53.880
A reckoning."

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:58.550
Now, do you think Captain Marvel will be able
to destroy the Space Stone with her Tesseract

00:06:58.550 --> 00:06:59.550
powers?

00:06:59.550 --> 00:07:03.550
And do you have any other theories on how
the MCU's newest hero will help the Avengers

00:07:03.550 --> 00:07:04.660
defeat Thanos?

